          <h4 class="font-bold text-sm md:text-base text-ink">Inverted Ceramic Plate</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
            Place an everyday lead-free ceramic side plate upside down over your ceramic bowl. Captures splatters completely, allows steam to escape from the rim, and introduces 0% plasticizers.
          </p>
          <span class="inline-block text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
            Rating: 100% Non-Toxic
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-emerald-500/30 space-y-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">&#128737;</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-sm md:text-base text-ink">Vented Silicone Dome</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
            Food-grade platinum silicone covers are heat resistant up to 230°C (450°F). Integrated vent holes prevent pressure build-up and will not warp, melt, or leach microplastics.
          </p>
          <span class="inline-block text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
            Rating: Reusable & Flexible
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-emerald-500/30 space-y-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">&#129531;</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-sm md:text-base text-ink">Unbleached Paper Towel</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
            Drape a single sheet of 100% recycled, chlorine-free unbleached paper towel loosely over the dish. Absorbs grease splatters directly while letting moisture vapor diffuse safely.
          </p>
          <span class="inline-block text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
            Rating: Disposable & Clean
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-emerald-500/30 space-y-3">
          <span class="text-2xl">&#129514;</span>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-sm md:text-base text-ink">Borosilicate Glass Tubs</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
            Reheat exclusively in lab-grade borosilicate glass (low thermal expansion). Completely non-porous; does not absorb oils, withstands 300°C+, and never pits or leaches chemicals.
          </p>
          <span class="inline-block text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
            Rating: Gold Standard Safe
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Golden Rules Callout -->
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-500/10 to-teal-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-ink space-y-2 mt-4">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
          The 3 Golden Rules of Safe Microwave Reheating:
        </h4>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-xs md:text-sm text-ink/80 space-y-1.5 leading-relaxed">
          <li><strong>Pop Before Power:</strong> Always pop open the steam vent valve or unclick the locking tabs before pressing start.</li>
          <li><strong>The 1-Inch Air Gap:</strong> Never allow plastic film, silicone, or covers to touch the surface of greasy or acidic food.</li>
          <li><strong>The 30-Second Rest:</strong> Wait 30 seconds after the microwave dings before removing the cover to allow internal pressure to equalize and prevent steam scalds.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

